---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Check the environment: config, devices, permissions, probe

Usage: pogo doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --deep
          Also open ports and perform the probe handshake

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

Checks that the config parses, devices are visible, ports are accessible, and the probe
firmware is compatible.

Examples:
  pogo doctor
  pogo doctor --deep -f json

Exit codes: 0 all checks passed or warned, 1 a check failed, 10 config invalid

JSON data: { checks: [ { id, status: pass|warn|fail, message, hint } ] }
